1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,800
I can’t tell my family what I want without feeling ungrateful.

2
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,150
Arjun puts the family pressure into his own words.

3
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:16,600
No one else sees this reflection.

4
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:20,550
Muse Spark's planned role is organizing themes.

5
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,000
Prepared example; no model is connected.

6
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:28,150
A possible reading is offered for him to check.

7
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:31,200
He says, “Not quite.”

8
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:36,100
He needs time to decide for himself.

9
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:47,400
The reflection changes to hold his correction.

10
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:52,000
His corrected theme keeps family context in view.

11
00:00:52,050 --> 00:00:56,200
Broader legal results are set aside.

12
00:00:56,650 --> 00:01:00,000
One prepared fictional perspective appears.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Ravi says a trusted friend helped him speak with family.

14
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:08,200
They share family pressure; their circumstances differ.

15
00:01:08,250 --> 00:01:11,800
Arjun has not said he has someone he trusts.

16
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:16,000
If he asks, it is for the group under an alias.

17
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:19,000
His private reflection is excluded.

18
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:23,900
Consent remains unchecked.

19
00:01:24,050 --> 00:01:26,800
He cancels and keeps the draft.

20
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,500
Nothing is sent.

21
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:34,400
For now, his words stay private.

22
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:39,000
He can ask for time before deciding.
